{%- comment -%}
  Participant directory — the ruled ledger on Network Participants.
  ====================================================================
  EVERY ROW IS RENDERED HERE, AT BUILD TIME, from src/_data/network_participants.json.
  js/ondc/network-participants.js only ever toggles `hidden` on nodes that
  already exist and writes text into elements that already exist. It never
  creates, moves or removes one. That is the same rule the Buyer App directory
  and the RFP ledger follow, and it is what stops the script fighting
  Bookshop's re-render while an editor types — hiding is idempotent, so a
  re-render costs nothing but a re-run.

  It is also why the filter tree, the role toggles and the filter chips are all
  drawn in full below and then hidden: a chip the script would have had to
  create is a chip that vanishes on the next keystroke in the editor.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section
  class="bk-directory"{% if anchor_id %} id="{{ anchor_id }}"{% endif %}
  data-screen-label="{{ screen_label | default: "Participant directory" }}"
  aria-label="{{ labels.aria | default: "Participant directory" }}"
  data-np-directory
  data-np-per-page="{{ per_page | default: 20 }}"
  data-np-noun="{{ labels.item_noun | default: "participant" }}"
  data-np-noun-plural="{{ labels.item_noun_plural | default: "participants" }}"
  data-np-export-name="{{ labels.export_filename | default: "ondc-network-participants" }}">

  {%- comment -%}
    Without JavaScript nothing can page, so paging must not be what decides
    whether a participant is on the page at all. Every row comes back, and the
    controls that would lie about what they do go away.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <noscript>
    <style>
      [data-np-directory] tr[data-np-row][hidden] { display: table-row; }
      [data-np-directory] [data-np-pagination],
      [data-np-directory] [data-np-rolebar],
      [data-np-directory] [data-np-search],
      [data-np-directory] [data-np-export],
      [data-np-directory] .bk-np-filters { display: none; }
      [data-np-directory] .bk-np-layout { display: block; }
    </style>
  </noscript>

  <div class="bk-np-toolbar">
    {% if directory_tabs.size > 0 %}
      <div class="bk-tabs bk-np-toplevel-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="{{ labels.tabs_aria | default: "Participant directories" }}">
        {% for tab in directory_tabs %}<a
            href="{{ tab.url }}"
            class="bk-tab{% if tab.current %} active{% endif %}"
            role="tab"
            aria-selected="{% if tab.current %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">{{ tab.label }}</a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if show_export %}
      <button type="button" class="bk-btn bk-btn-ghost" data-np-export>{{ export_label | default: "Export CSV" }}</button>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="bk-np-layout">
    {%- comment -%}
      The category tree is the official ONDC taxonomy, from
      src/_data/np_categories.json. Every branch is drawn; the script hides the
      ones the visible list has no rows for, because a greyed-out option
      asserts "no participants" when the truth is "none in this list".
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <aside class="bk-np-filters" aria-label="{{ labels.filters | default: "Filter by category" }}">
      <div class="bk-np-filter-group">
        <div class="bk-eyebrow">{{ labels.category_heading | default: "Category" }}</div>
        <div data-np-tree>
          {% assign parents = np_categories.categories | where: "parent", "" %}
          {% for parent in parents %}
            {% assign children = np_categories.categories | where: "parent", parent.name %}
            {% assign kids_id = "npKids-" | append: forloop.index %}
            <div class="bk-np-cat" data-cat="{{ parent.name | escape }}" data-np-branch hidden>
              <div class="bk-np-cat-row">
                <input
                  type="checkbox"
                  class="npCat"
                  id="{{ kids_id }}-box"
                  value="{{ parent.name | escape }}"
                  data-np-cat
                  aria-label="{{ parent.name | escape }}">
                {%- comment -%}
                  Two controls, deliberately not one. The checkbox selects the
                  whole category; the rest of the row is a button that expands
                  it. Folded into a <summary> instead, one click on the
                  checkbox would both tick the box and collapse the branch.
                  A branch with nothing under it gets a label rather than a
                  button: an expander onto an empty box is a promise it cannot
                  keep.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {% if children.size > 0 %}<button
                    type="button"
                    class="bk-np-cat-toggle"
                    aria-expanded="false"
                    aria-controls="{{ kids_id }}">
                    <span class="bk-np-chk-label">{{ parent.name }}</span>
                    <span class="bk-np-chk-count" data-np-count>0</span>
                    <svg class="bk-np-cat-chev" width="9" height="6" viewBox="0 0 8 5" fill="none"
                      stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"
                      stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M1 1l3 3 3-3"></path></svg>
                  </button>
                {% else %}<label class="bk-np-cat-toggle is-leaf" for="{{ kids_id }}-box">
                    <span class="bk-np-chk-label">{{ parent.name }}</span>
                    <span class="bk-np-chk-count" data-np-count>0</span>
                  </label>
                {% endif %}
              </div>
              {% if children.size > 0 %}
                <div class="bk-np-cat-kids" id="{{ kids_id }}" hidden>
                  {% for child in children %}
                    <label class="bk-np-chk" data-np-leaf hidden>
                      <input
                        type="checkbox"
                        class="npSub"
                        value="{{ child.name | escape }}"
                        data-np-sub
                        data-parent="{{ parent.name | escape }}">
                      <span class="bk-np-chk-label">{{ child.name }}</span>
                      <span class="bk-np-chk-count" data-np-count>0</span>
                    </label>
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="bk-np-results">
      <input
        type="search"
        class="bk-directory-input"
        data-np-search
        aria-label="{{ labels.search | default: "Search participants" }}"
        placeholder="{{ search_placeholder | default: "Search by name, category, contact or website" }}"
        autocomplete="off">

      {%- comment -%}
        Two long list names side by side ate the results row and wrapped at
        390px. One trigger carrying the current list, opening to both, says the
        same thing in a third of the width.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% if lists.size > 1 %}
        <details class="bk-np-listdrop" data-np-listdrop>
          <summary aria-label="{{ labels.list_switch | default: "Participant list" }}"><span data-np-tablabel>{{ lists[0].label }}</span>
            <svg class="nav-drop-chev" width="8" height="5" viewBox="0 0 8 5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M1 1l3 3 3-3"></path>
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="bk-np-listdrop-menu">
            {% for list in lists %}<button
                type="button"
                class="np-tab{% if forloop.first %} active{% endif %}"
                data-np-tab="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
                data-np-note="{{ list.note | escape }}"{% if forloop.first %} aria-current="true"{% endif %}>{{ list.label }}</button>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        </details>
      {% endif %}
      {%- comment -%}
        Kept whenever there is more than one list, even if THIS list's note is
        empty, because switching lists writes the next one's note into it. A
        single-list directory with nothing to say drops the element rather than
        leaving an empty paragraph holding its margin open.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign show_note = false -%}
      {%- if lists.size > 1 -%}{%- assign show_note = true -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if lists[0].note != blank -%}{%- assign show_note = true -%}{%- endif -%}
      {% if show_note %}<p class="bk-np-tabnote" data-np-tabnote>{{ lists[0].note }}</p>{% endif %}

      <div class="bk-np-filterbar">
        <div class="bk-np-rolebar" data-np-rolebar role="group" aria-label="{{ labels.roles | default: "Filter by role" }}">
          {% for role in np_roles.roles %}
            <button
              type="button"
              class="bk-np-role"
              data-np-role="{{ role.role_value | escape }}"
              aria-pressed="false"
              hidden>
              {% if role.role_key != role.role_full %}<span class="bk-np-key">{{ role.role_key }}</span>{% endif %}
              <span class="bk-np-role-t">{{ role.role_label }}</span>
              <span class="bk-np-role-n" data-np-count>0</span>
            </button>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="bk-directory-summary" data-np-caption role="status"></p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        One chip per filter the reader could possibly have on, all hidden. The
        script unhides the ones that are ticked. Creating them on the fly would
        break the no-new-nodes rule this whole section is built on.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="bk-np-chips" data-np-chips hidden aria-label="{{ labels.active_filters | default: "Active filters" }}">
        {% for role in np_roles.roles %}
          <button type="button" class="bk-np-chip" data-np-chip="role" data-value="{{ role.role_value | escape }}" hidden>{{ role.role_label }}<span aria-hidden="true">&#10005;</span><span class="bk-sr-only"> — {{ labels.remove_filter | default: "remove this filter" }}</span></button>
        {% endfor %}
        {% for cat in np_categories.categories %}
          <button type="button" class="bk-np-chip" data-np-chip="{% if cat.parent == "" %}cat{% else %}sub{% endif %}" data-value="{{ cat.name | escape }}" hidden>{{ cat.name }}<span aria-hidden="true">&#10005;</span><span class="bk-sr-only"> — {{ labels.remove_filter | default: "remove this filter" }}</span></button>
        {% endfor %}
        <button type="button" class="bk-np-chip-clear" data-np-clear hidden>{{ labels.clear_all | default: "Clear all" }}</button>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Column labels are the ledger's own. "Brand Logo" and "Link" are not
        facts a reader looks up, they are parts of Participant and Contact.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="bk-np-table-wrap">
        <table class="bk-np-table">
          <colgroup>
            <col style="width:29%">
            <col style="width:12%">
            <col style="width:31%">
            <col style="width:28%">
          </colgroup>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">{{ labels.col_participant | default: "Participant" }}</th>
              <th scope="col">{{ labels.col_role | default: "Role" }}</th>
              <th scope="col">{{ labels.col_categories | default: "Categories" }}</th>
              <th scope="col">{{ labels.col_contact | default: "Contact" }}</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          {%- comment -%}
            Rows past the first page ship hidden. The script would hide them a
            moment later anyway, but "a moment later" is 494 rows painted and
            then collapsed to 20 — a layout shift the length of the page. The
            <noscript> rule below hands all of them back when there is no
            script to do the paging.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {% assign page_size = per_page | default: 20 | plus: 0 %}
          {%- comment -%}
            Which data file each option in the "Which participants" dropdown
            reads. Written out rather than looked up dynamically because Liquid
            cannot resolve a global by a name held in a variable — and because
            being explicit is what makes a fourth directory two lines here plus
            one option in the .bookshop.yml, instead of a puzzle.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {% for list in lists %}
            {% case list.source %}
              {% when "ecosystem" %}{% assign rows = ecosystem_participants.participants %}
              {% when "integrated" %}{% assign rows = network_participants.integrated %}
              {% else %}{% assign rows = network_participants.key %}
            {% endcase %}
            {% if list.sort != "as_listed" %}{% assign rows = rows | sort_natural: "name" %}{% endif %}
            <tbody data-np-body data-np-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}"{% unless forloop.first %} hidden{% endunless %}>
              {%- for p in rows %}
                {%- comment -%}
                  Searched against every source value, not only the printed
                  ones: a full role name and a URL fragment both find their
                  row even though the table prints a key and the word
                  "Website". Built once here so the script only has to look at
                  one lower-cased string per row.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign role_text = p.roles | join: " " -%}
                {%- assign cat_text = p.categories | join: " " -%}
                {%- capture row_text -%}
                  {{ p.name }} {{ p.enabled_by }} {{ p.spoc }} {{ p.email }} {{ p.phone }} {{ p.website }} {{ role_text }} {{ cat_text }}
                {%- endcapture -%}
<tr data-np-row{% if forloop.index > page_size %} hidden{% endif %} data-np-roles="{{ p.roles | join: "|" | escape }}" data-np-cats="{{ p.categories | join: "|" | escape }}" data-np-name="{{ p.name | escape }}" data-np-enabled="{{ p.enabled_by | escape }}" data-np-text="{{ row_text | strip | downcase | escape }}">
                  <td class="bk-np-who" data-label="{{ labels.col_participant | default: "Participant" }}"><span class="bk-np-whoin">
                      {%- if p.logo -%}<img src="{{ p.logo }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-np-logo data-np-name="{{ p.name | escape }}">
                      {%- else -%}{%- assign ini = p.initials -%}{%- if ini == blank -%}{%- assign ini = p.name | slice: 0, 2 | upcase -%}{%- endif -%}<span class="bk-np-monogram" aria-hidden="true">{{ ini }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      <span class="bk-np-name">{{ p.name }}{% if p.enabled_by %}<span class="bk-np-enabled">{{ labels.enabled_by | default: "Enabled by" }} {{ p.enabled_by }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
                    </span></td>
                  <td class="bk-np-roles" data-label="{{ labels.col_role | default: "Role" }}">
                    {%- if p.roles.size == 0 -%}<span class="bk-np-none" aria-hidden="true">&#8212;</span><span class="bk-sr-only">{{ labels.not_recorded | default: "Not recorded" }}</span>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- for r in p.roles -%}
                        {%- assign rk = np_roles.roles | where: "role_value", r | first -%}
                        {%- if rk -%}<abbr class="bk-np-key" title="{{ rk.role_full | escape }}">{{ rk.role_key }}</abbr>
                        {%- else -%}<span class="bk-np-key">{{ r }}</span>
                        {%- endif -%}{%- unless forloop.last %} {% endunless -%}
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
</td>
                  <td class="bk-np-cats" data-label="{{ labels.col_categories | default: "Categories" }}">
                    {%- if p.categories.size == 0 -%}<span class="bk-np-none" aria-hidden="true">&#8212;</span><span class="bk-sr-only">{{ labels.not_recorded | default: "Not recorded" }}</span>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- for c in p.categories limit: 3 -%}<span class="bk-np-cat-chip">{{ c }}</span>{% unless forloop.last %} {% endunless %}{%- endfor -%}
                      {%- if p.categories.size > 3 -%}
                        <span class="bk-np-cat-rest" hidden>{% for c in p.categories offset: 3 %}<span class="bk-np-cat-chip">{{ c }}</span>{% unless forloop.last %} {% endunless %}{% endfor %}</span>
                        <button type="button" class="bk-np-more" aria-expanded="false"><span class="bk-np-more-in">+{{ p.categories.size | minus: 3 }}</span><span class="bk-np-more-out">{{ labels.fewer | default: "Fewer" }}</span><span class="bk-sr-only"> {{ labels.col_categories | default: "categories" | downcase }}</span></button>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
</td>
                  <td class="bk-np-contact" data-label="{{ labels.col_contact | default: "Contact" }}">
                    {%- assign has_action = false -%}
                    {%- if p.email != "" or p.phone != "" or p.website != "" -%}{%- assign has_action = true -%}{%- endif -%}
                    {%- if p.spoc == "" and has_action == false -%}<span class="bk-np-none" aria-hidden="true">&#8212;</span><span class="bk-sr-only">{{ labels.not_recorded | default: "Not recorded" }}</span>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- if p.spoc != "" -%}<span class="bk-np-contact-line bk-np-spoc">{{ p.spoc }}</span>{%- endif -%}
                      {%- if has_action -%}<span class="bk-np-contact-line">
                        {%- assign first = true -%}
                        {%- if p.email != "" -%}<a class="bk-ul" href="mailto:{{ p.email }}">{{ labels.email | default: "Email" }}<span class="bk-sr-only"> {{ p.name }}</span></a>{%- assign first = false -%}{%- endif -%}
                        {%- if p.phone != "" -%}{% unless first %} <span class="bk-np-sep" aria-hidden="true">&#183;</span> {% endunless %}<a class="bk-ul" href="tel:{{ p.phone | remove: " " }}">{{ labels.call | default: "Call" }}<span class="bk-sr-only"> {{ p.name }}</span></a>{%- assign first = false -%}{%- endif -%}
                        {%- if p.website != "" -%}{% unless first %} <span class="bk-np-sep" aria-hidden="true">&#183;</span> {% endunless %}<a class="bk-ul" href="{{ p.website }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ labels.website | default: "Website" }}<span class="bk-sr-only"> {{ labels.website_sr | default: "for" }} {{ p.name }}</span></a>{%- endif -%}
                      </span>{%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
</td>
                </tr>
              {%- endfor %}
              <tr data-np-empty hidden>
                <td colspan="4" class="np-empty">{{ labels.empty | default: "No participants match these filters. Remove one above to widen the search." }}</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          {% endfor %}
        </table>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Seven number slots and two gaps, all hidden. The script fills in the
        page numbers it needs — first, last, current and its neighbours — and
        hides the rest, so paging never adds a node either.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="bk-np-pagination" data-np-pagination>
        <div class="bk-np-rpp">
          <label for="{{ anchor_id | default: "np" }}-rpp">{{ labels.rows_per_page | default: "Rows per page" }}</label>
          <select id="{{ anchor_id | default: "np" }}-rpp" data-np-rpp>
            {% assign choices = per_page_choices | default: "20, 30, 50, 100" | split: "," %}
            {% for c in choices %}{% assign cv = c | strip %}<option value="{{ cv }}"{% if cv == per_page %} selected{% endif %}>{{ cv }}</option>{% endfor %}
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="bk-np-pagenums">
          <button type="button" data-np-prev aria-label="{{ labels.prev | default: "Previous page" }}">&lsaquo;</button>
          <button type="button" data-np-num hidden></button>
          <span class="bk-np-ellipsis" data-np-gap hidden>&hellip;</span>
          <button type="button" data-np-num hidden></button>
          <button type="button" data-np-num hidden></button>
          <button type="button" data-np-num hidden></button>
          <span class="bk-np-ellipsis" data-np-gap hidden>&hellip;</span>
          <button type="button" data-np-num hidden></button>
          <button type="button" data-np-next aria-label="{{ labels.next | default: "Next page" }}">&rsaquo;</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if disclaimer %}
    <p class="bk-note" style="margin-top:32px">{{ disclaimer }}</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>
